  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "scene_Ia7wkIKQQl",
      "type": "slide",
      "order": 1,
      "title": "Welcome & Course Overview",
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_AYUGaLDB",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_ThM6NXYf"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_cluJFXd1",
          "text": "Good morning, everyone! I’m Ms. Emma Clarke, and I’m excited to welcome you to our Introduction to HTML course. Today we’ll get an overview of what HTML is, why it matters, and what you’ll achieve by the end of this class.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_SZ8KQywK",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_SdfpoesI"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_UKT4un6p",
          "text": "First, let’s talk about the question on the screen: “What is HTML and why it matters for web development?” HTML, or HyperText Markup Language, is the backbone of every webpage—it tells browsers how to structure text, images, links, and more. Without HTML, the web would be just a collection of raw files with no meaning.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_rkX97Guy",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_SdfpoesI"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_tdUf0AGf",
          "text": "Next, look at the three main objectives listed here: we’ll learn the basic tags, understand how to build a simple page, and explore how HTML fits into the larger web development workflow. By the end of the course, you’ll be able to create your own functional web pages from scratch.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_NXT6IMY_",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_SdfpoesI"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_Ajgg79wS",
          "text": "Finally, the structure of our upcoming lessons will follow a clear pattern: a brief concept introduction, a hands‑on example, and a short practice activity. Keep that in mind as we move forward, and feel free to ask questions at any point.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_pNKAY6yG",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_ThM6NXYf"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_uKcZbQk1",
          "text": "That’s our roadmap for today—understanding HTML’s role, our learning goals, and how we’ll proceed. Let’s dive in!",
          "type": "speech"
        }
      ],
