    {
      "id": "scene_LFXyOdKfVC",
      "type": "quiz",
      "order": 5,
      "title": "Quick Check: Basic Tags",
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_ce-FZ5vE",
          "text": "Hello everyone! It's time for a quick check on the basic HTML tags we just covered. You'll see two questions—one single‑answer and one where you can pick all that apply. Read each option carefully, then choose the best answer.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_uIDSgV6C",
          "text": "Remember, the top‑level heading tag is <h1>, and when you're building a simple paragraph, the <p> element is the most appropriate. Elements like <div> and <section> can hold blocks of content, but they aren't specifically meant for a single paragraph, while <span> is an inline tag for small pieces of text.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_v4x0bpYq",
          "text": "Take your time, and don't worry if you're unsure—this is just a chance to see how well the concepts are sticking. Once you’ve answered, we’ll review the reasoning together.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_VY599GLt",
          "type": "discussion",
          "topic": "Why is it important to choose the most semantically correct HTML tag for headings and paragraphs?",
          "prompt": "Think about how browsers and assistive technologies use these tags, and share any ‘what if’ scenarios you’re curious about.",
          "agentId": "gen-server-2"
        }
      ],
      "content": {
        "type": "quiz",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "q1",
            "type": "single",
            "answer": [
              "A"
            ],
            "points": 5,
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "<h1>"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "<heading>"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "<title>"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "<head>"
              }
            ],
            "analysis": "The <h1> tag defines the most important heading. <heading> is not a valid HTML tag, <title> defines the page title in the head section, and <head> is a container for meta-information.",
            "question": "Which HTML tag is used to create a top-level heading?",
            "hasAnswer": true
          },
          {
            "id": "q2",
            "type": "multiple",
            "answer": [
              "A",
              "B"
            ],
            "points": 7,
            "options": [
              {
                "value": "A",
                "label": "<p>"
              },
              {
                "value": "B",
                "label": "<div>"
              },
              {
                "value": "C",
                "label": "<span>"
              },
              {
                "value": "D",
                "label": "<section>"
              }
            ],
            "analysis": "<p> is the semantic element for a paragraph. <div> can also be used to group block‑level content, including paragraphs, though it lacks semantic meaning. <span> is inline and not suitable for a full paragraph, and <section> is meant for thematic grouping, not a single paragraph.",
            "question": "Select all HTML elements that are appropriate for structuring a basic paragraph of text (choose all that apply).",
            "hasAnswer": true
          }
        ]
      },
      "stageId": "BIJsvMsYgh",
