    {
      "id": "scene_1TO32ZIQzm",
      "type": "slide",
      "order": 9,
      "title": "Semantic HTML & Good Practices",
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_cJDQwatg",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_ee5eApH9"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_rdP0xaYA",
          "text": "Alright everyone, let’s dive into Semantic HTML and good coding practices. This helps us write pages that are both understandable to browsers and accessible to users.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_N8p8ioWU",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_cGT0JUK3"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_HYAqcYvA",
          "text": "First, notice the list of semantic elements: <header>, <nav>, <main>, <section>, <article>, and <footer>. These tags describe the purpose of each part of the page, making the structure clear.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_kVZaF6TE",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_cGT0JUK3"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_eSTraLZV",
          "text": "Why does that matter? Semantic tags improve accessibility because screen readers can announce sections correctly, and they boost SEO since search engines understand the content hierarchy.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_JlU-0BoP",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_cGT0JUK3"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_zKSczoHC",
          "text": "Lastly, clean code formatting—consistent indentation and meaningful IDs or class names—makes our HTML easier to read, maintain, and collaborate on.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_W8r3UejL",
          "text": "To recap, we covered the key semantic elements, their benefits for accessibility and SEO, and the importance of tidy code conventions. Any quick questions before we move on?",
          "type": "speech"
        }
      ],
      "content": {
