    {
      "id": "scene_EEC012qHuj",
      "type": "quiz",
      "order": 10,
      "title": "Final Knowledge Check",
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_3XuqoyRf",
          "text": "Alright, it's time for our final knowledge check! This short quiz will bring together everything we've learned about semantic tags, list structures, and form controls. Read each question carefully and choose the best answer.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_JTPbd_4d",
          "text": "Remember, the <nav> element is designed specifically for navigation links, while <section> groups related content, <article> represents a self‑contained composition, and <aside> holds tangential information. Keep that in mind for the first question.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_YtvJa3-9",
          "text": "For lists, think about the purpose: <ul> and <ol> are for unordered and ordered lists of items, <dl> is for definition lists, and a <table> is for tabular data, not typical list items. And when you get to the form controls, recall that <input type=\"text\"> captures short text, <textarea> handles longer multi‑line input, and <select> lets users pick from a set of options.",
          "type": "speech"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_xFNEtYV9",
          "text": "Good luck! Once you’ve answered, we’ll review the correct responses together and highlight any common pitfalls.",
          "type": "speech"
        }
      ],
